T1100 M82: send the ROMv4 patch before the firmware sections.

The gen4m vendor flow hands the ROMv4 patch to the MCU ROM *before* it
downloads the WLAN RAM-code sections. Our M22 path sent it afterwards,
and on this ROM the patch CIDs are then not answered at all: the M81 log
shows PATCH_SEMAPHORE_CONTROL(get) and PATCH_START both timing out
(wlanImageSectionDownloadStatus returns WLAN_STATUS_FAILURE = 0xC0000001)
and the MCU resets (WCIR=0), so the following WIFI_START goes into a dead
MCU and READY never rises.

Move t1100_rom_patch_send() to just before the download; keep it behind
t1100_rom_patch_mcif so both orders can still be compared.

--- a/common/wlan_lib.c
+++ b/common/wlan_lib.c
@@ -1097,6 +1097,16 @@
 		/* 3. FW download here */
 		DBGLOG(INIT, TRACE, "FW download start...\n");
 
+		/*
+		 * T1100 M82: the vendor gen4m flow hands the ROMv4 patch to the
+		 * MCU *before* the firmware sections. After the sections the ROM
+		 * no longer answers the patch CIDs (M81: timeout 0xC0000001).
+		 */
+		if (t1100_rom_patch_mcif) {
+			t1100_rom_patch_send(prAdapter);
+			t1100_hif_state(prAdapter, "after-rompatch");
+		}
+
 #if CFG_ENABLE_FW_DIVIDED_DOWNLOAD
 		/* 3a. parse file header for decision of divided firmware download or not */
 		prFwHead = (P_FIRMWARE_DIVIDED_DOWNLOAD_T)prFwBuffer;
@@ -1155,8 +1165,7 @@
 		 * T1100 M22: hand the ROMv4 patch to the MCU ROM before asking it
 		 * to jump into the WLAN RAM code (see t1100_rom_patch_send()).
 		 */
-		t1100_rom_patch_send(prAdapter);
-		t1100_hif_state(prAdapter, "after-rompatch");
+		/* T1100 M82: the ROM patch is sent before the download now. */
 #endif
 
 		if (t1100_reset_before_start) {
